From 16db618ac19d2bc7a51a3d41205a55b05e880a76 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gl11tchy <gl11tchy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 01:57:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] feat(sigil): make Sigil Neon a layout, not only a palette
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The theme now reshapes the TUI. Every other theme is untouched.

- appearance: a Sigil profile — no filled prompt card, wider outer
  margins, a dot bullet, shell-style command headers
- prompt widget: PromptStyle::rule_chrome — the composer is a hairline
  above the text and its info line below, with the accent bar as the
  left edge, instead of a box
- scrollback: the speaker is carried in the margin — a violet bar for
  the human's turn, mint for the agent's
- welcome: a wordmark and one rule in place of the braille art and the
  bordered hero box
- context: the meter is the resting state, not a hover reveal
